<article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10">
  <EthosWeb.GuideBreadcrumb.guide_breadcrumb guide={@guide} />

  <header class="mt-2">
    <h1 class="font-display text-display-sm">{@guide.title}</h1>
    {live_render(@conn, EthosWeb.SocialLive,
      id: "social-guide-#{@guide.id}",
      session: %{"subject_type" => "guide", "subject_id" => @guide.id}
    )}
    <p class="mt-1 text-ink-muted">{@guide.destination}</p>
    <p :for={c <- @collections} class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">
      Part of <.link navigate={~p"/c/#{c.slug}"} class="underline">{c.title}</.link>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section :if={(@guide.photos || []) != []} class="mt-6">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">
        Pictures from {@guide.destination |> String.split(",") |> List.first()}
      </h2>
      <.link navigate={~p"/g/#{@guide.slug}/photos"} class="text-sm underline">
        See all {length(@guide.photos)} photos →
      </.link>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-4 gap-2">
      <.link :for={p <- Enum.take(@guide.photos, 4)} navigate={~p"/g/#{@guide.slug}/photos"}>
        <img
          src={p["thumb"]}
          alt={p["title"]}
          loading="lazy"
          class="aspect-square w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
        />
      </.link>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div :if={@guide.intro} class="prose mt-6">{EthosWeb.Markdown.render(@guide.intro)}</div>

  <%!-- The generic GetYourGuide CTA is the FALLBACK. A page whose geography
        resolves to a configured affiliate locale gets the widget from the app
        layout instead — one unit per page, above or below the content
        depending on the locale's :placement (Rome is :top). This condition
        is not a hardcoded state check, so Rome's aside becomes Rome's widget
        the day a Rome entry lands in the registry, with no edit here.

        It asks "will a unit render?", NOT "did a locale resolve?" — the two
        differ for a locale whose :network has no component clause yet, and
        asking the weaker question suppressed this fallback on pages that then
        rendered no widget either. `unit_renders?/1` is the same predicate the
        components use.

        The house ad (EthosWeb.HouseAd) renders under this same "no affiliate
        widget" condition, so without the second clause below a guide page
        outside New York and Italy would carry both — two ad-shaped units.
        The house ad is specific and internal to Ethos; this CTA is a generic
        sponsored link that belongs precisely where GetYourGuide has no
        campaign. The house ad takes precedence, and this remains the
        fallback for when there is no ad to show (empty pool, no usable
        photograph).

        The flag (`EthosWeb.Affiliate.enabled?/0`) is now the first clause:
        with affiliates off, this generic sponsored CTA must not appear
        either, even on pages where a widget would otherwise have rendered —
        otherwise turning affiliates off would turn this CTA ON in exactly
        those places. --%>
  <aside
    :if={
      EthosWeb.Affiliate.enabled?() and
        not EthosWeb.Affiliate.unit_renders?(assigns) and
        is_nil(EthosWeb.HouseAd.for_page(assigns))
    }
    class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="font-semibold">Planning your own trip?</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Browse tours, skip-the-line tickets, and day trips on GetYourGuide — booking
        through this link supports Ethos.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a
      href={gyg_partner_url()}
      rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"
      target="_blank"
      class="shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-amber-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-amber-600"
    >
      Explore tours →
    </a>
  </aside>

  <ol class="mt-8 space-y-4">
    <li
      :for={entry <- @entries}
      id={"entry-#{entry.id}"}
      class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"
    >
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-lg">
            <%= cond do %>
              <% match?(%{slug: _}, entry.place) -> %>
                <.link navigate={~p"/p/#{entry.place.slug}"} class="hover:underline">
                  {entry.name}
                </.link>
              <% entry.enrichment && entry.enrichment["official_url"] &&
                   EthosWeb.Url.safe_http?(entry.enrichment["official_url"]) -> %>
                <a href={entry.enrichment["official_url"]} class="hover:underline" rel="nofollow">
                  {entry.name}
                </a>
              <% true -> %>
                {entry.name}
            <% end %>
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
            {entry.kind}
            <span :if={entry.day}>· day {entry.day}</span>
            <span :if={verdict_badge(entry.verdict)}>· {verdict_badge(entry.verdict)}</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-copy-url={entry_share_url(@guide, entry)}
          class="shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-line px-2 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted hover:bg-surface-raised"
        >
          Copy link
        </button>
      </div>

      <p :if={entry.note} class="mt-2">{entry.note}</p>

      <a
        :if={EthosWeb.Affiliate.enabled?() and EthosWeb.Url.safe_http?(entry.booking_url)}
        href={entry.booking_url}
        rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"
        target="_blank"
        class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-amber-600"
      >
        {entry.booking_label || "Book this"} →
      </a>

      <p :if={entry.credited_user_id} class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-muted">
        added from a reader suggestion
      </p>

      <div :if={@research[entry.id]} class="mt-3 rounded-md bg-surface-raised p-3 text-sm">
        <p class="font-medium text-ink-muted">Fresh research</p>
        <ul class="mt-1 space-y-1">
          <li :for={r <- @research[entry.id]["results"]}>
            <%= if EthosWeb.Url.safe_http?(r["url"]) do %>
              <a href={r["url"]} class="underline" rel="nofollow">{r["title"] || r["url"]}</a>
            <% else %>
              <span>{r["title"] || r["url"]}</span>
            <% end %>
            <span :if={r["snippet"]} class="text-ink-muted">— {r["snippet"]}</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <form
        :if={Ethos.Accounts.admin?(@current_user)}
        action={~p"/g/#{@guide.slug}/entries/#{entry.id}/research"}
        method="post"
        class="mt-2"
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={Plug.CSRFProtection.get_csrf_token()} />
        <button class="text-xs underline text-ink-muted">Research this</button>
      </form>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <section :for={section <- @guide.sections || []} class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">{section["heading"]}</h2>
    <div class="prose mt-2">{EthosWeb.Markdown.render(section["body"])}</div>
  </section>

  <section :if={(@guide.faq || []) != []} class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <dl class="mt-3 space-y-4">
      <div :for={item <- @guide.faq}>
        <dt class="font-medium">{Map.get(item, "question", "")}</dt>
        <dd class="text-ink-muted mt-1">{Map.get(item, "answer", "")}</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <%!-- This page's original disclosure. Unlike the amber aside above, this
        line is not purely the unit's fallback: it also covers the entries'
        own sponsored `booking_url` links (rel="sponsored nofollow noopener",
        above), which the widget's disclosure never mentions — that one
        scopes itself to "tours and activities shown above", i.e. the widget
        alone. So this line stands whenever there is something on the page it
        uniquely covers: either the unit doesn't render (its disclosure isn't
        here to share the load), or the page has a sponsored entry link the
        unit's disclosure says nothing about. Only when neither is true —
        the unit renders AND no entry has a booking_url — would this be a
        second disclosure for the same thing, and only then is it suppressed.

        `EthosWeb.Affiliate.enabled?/0` is ANDed over the whole expression,
        not pushed into either branch of the `or`: with affiliates off, no
        link on this page earns a commission, so the disclosure must not
        appear regardless of what the two branches below would otherwise
        say. --%>
  <p
    :if={
      EthosWeb.Affiliate.enabled?() and
        (not EthosWeb.Affiliate.unit_renders?(assigns) or
           Enum.any?(@entries, &EthosWeb.Url.safe_http?(&1.booking_url)))
    }
    class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-muted"
  >
    Some booking links on this page earn Ethos a commission at no extra cost to you.
  </p>

  <EthosWeb.FoliagePanel.foliage_panel foliage={@foliage} />

  <EthosWeb.ConnectedPages.connected_pages connected={@connected} />

  <footer class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4 border-t border-line pt-6">
    <.link
      navigate={~p"/g/#{@guide.slug}/suggest"}
      class="rounded-md bg-accent px-4 py-2 text-accent-ink text-sm"
    >
      Suggest a place
    </.link>
    <.link
      :if={Ethos.Accounts.admin?(@current_user)}
      navigate={~p"/guides/new"}
      class="rounded-md border border-line px-4 py-2 text-sm"
    >
      Make your own guide
    </.link>
  </footer>
</article>
